how (T7-T8-T9) if T8 is drawn. This path maximizes meld opportunities and aligns with scoring patterns like Pure Straight or Quadruple Chow.  \nReason: B8 is critical for a third chow in dots, and playing it reduces risk of others claiming it while preserving flexibility for future melds.  \nAnswer: Play B8"}
